 "notes": "Plate at 200 ft/inch. Names as printed: OBANNION (no apostrophe), LEOLIE, DREMAN (no suffix seen), BRASHEARS. Powers, Sullivan, Allen and Elmore names are printed on 37L. Ralston is printed RALSTON west of Spring Grove and AVE. 60' east of it; the two pieces meet Spring Grove ~35 px apart. Johnson Street north of Arlington is printed only 'ST.' (taken as Johnson, continuous). Primrose east of Colerain is unlabelled (1904 key map calls it Erie Av.). No bracketed old names seen. Not picked (unnamed): two 'NO NAME' streets running SE from Archibald Street to Mill Creek; an unnamed stub from the top edge across Mill Creek to Ludlow Avenue (~2490,190); a narrow unnamed passage (6 in. water pipe) from Ludlow (~2865,2265) to Streng (~2865,2945); a street printed only 'ROAD' east of Colerain at ~(2700,5360) along the canal bed. Archibald Street and Ludlow Avenue run off the top edge; Lafayette Avenue's upper piece at the right edge (5650-5900, 1430-2300) meets no other street. Eyre Avenue's SE 50 ft leg dead-ends at the tract corner."
